{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, keep the installed curl package at its current version during system updates.","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl was initially installed at 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.8 and not held. The executor applied an APT/dpkg hold, confirmed the same installed version, and a simulated upgrade scheduled no curl replacement. After a verified reboot, curl remained installed at that version, executable, held, and excluded from the simulated upgrade.","evidence_ids":["cmd-62950496d2e8483a","cmd-f1f3c918602b4e05","cmd-a9019dc70e7447aa","cmd-a9da2606c97144c0"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Applying the curl hold directly satisfied the task (cmd-f1f3c918602b4e05), and the reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol (cmd-9581c5e3cc0b4b6c). All other commands were read-only verification or bounded waiting; the connection reset occurred during the expected reboot transition. Post-execution observations show healthy dpkg state, no failed services, and no unexplained residue or unsafe exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1f3c918602b4e05","cmd-9581c5e3cc0b4b6c","cmd-4d3d9bf71124416f","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task is satisfied. curl was held at its original installed version, excluded from simulated updates, and the hold persisted across reboot. The mandatory restart evidence is coherent: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and node1 recovered running with curl and its hold intact. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Update behavior was tested with `apt-get -s upgrade` rather than by applying a real system update; the simulation directly shows that curl would not be replaced while avoiding unrelated package changes."]}
